Copy software-decoded frames into real-sized GBM buffers

dup_gst_memory_as_dmabuf allocates an R8 GBM BO that is one pixel high
and as wide as the frame's byte count - over 6 MB wide for a 1080p RGB
frame. Drivers with an ordinary maximum texture size refuse that (virgl
in QEMU does), so every software-decoded frame failed to upload.

For single-plane frames, allocate a BO with the frame's own width, height
and DRM format instead, copy it row by row, and import it with the BO's
stride as the pitch. DMA-BUF frames from hardware decoders are untouched.

Signed-off-by: Mira <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/src/plugins/gstreamer_video_player/frame.c
+++ b/src/plugins/gstreamer_video_player/frame.c
@@ -566,6 +566,89 @@
